itle":"Cave","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz9g","title":"Dead City","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz3g","title":"Dragon's lair","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz3g","title":"Foothills","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz7g","title":"Great Magician's Catacomb","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz4g","title":"Khadaganian expedition camp","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz5g","title":"Lizard hermit's home","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz6g","title":"Middle Mountains","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz4g","title":"Remote Mountains","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz1g","title":"Ruins","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz8g","title":"Sands","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz6g","title":"Sheivar settlement","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz7g","title":"The river and the islands","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz2g","title":"The road to the Witch","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/gz10g","title":"Tunnel","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz1g","title":"Village","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"map/bz2g","title":"Witch's cave","variant":""}],"title":"Locations"}],"versions":[{"guide":"","html":"<article><h1>Gipath</h1><h2>Setting</h2><p>Gipath is an unclaimed allod of scattered ruins, mountains and wilderness. Its small human village shares the island with goblins, orcs and lizardmen. The apparent remoteness hides older history: Joon remains, the Dead City and the dwelling of a Great Magician all lie on the same island. [1, 2, 3]</p><h2>Events in Cursed Lands</h2><p><a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a> begins his search for his identity here. The village leaders’ disputes, <a href=\"wiki://character/witch\">Estera</a>’s advice and encounters with the island’s other peoples lead him to <a href=\"wiki://character/rick\">Tka Rik (Tka-Lithan Richti-Nik)</a>. Gipath is also the destination of his return: the truth about At-Zako and the struggle against the Curse bring the story back beneath its ruins. [4, 5, 6, 7]</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>Based on the original game dialogue and world descriptions. Source numbers refer to the scenes listed below.</p><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>#</th><th>Sources</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>World description · Gipath (allod gipat)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>World description · Dead City (zone gz9g)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/witch\">Estera</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a> (briefing z11_1)</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/sheriff\">Gort the Skullcrusher</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/elder\">Erfar the Silvertongue</a> (briefing s1)</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/rick\">Tka Rik (Tka-Lithan Richti-Nik)</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a> (briefing r36)</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/rick\">Tka Rik (Tka-Lithan Richti-Nik)</a> (briefing r72_4)</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/rick\">Tka Rik (Tka-Lithan Richti-Nik)</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/deva\">Lu-a-Jalla</a> (briefing r72_6)</td></tr></table><h2>Inhabitants</h2><table data-columns=\"1\"><tr><th>Related page</th></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/daughter\">Airy the Stubborn</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/smith\">Babur the Tightfist</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/merc4\">Eila the Sandwoman</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/elder\">Erfar the Silvertongue</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/witch\">Estera</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/hwleader\">Expedition commander</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/bgoblinc\">GoGo</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/sheriff\">Gort the Skullcrusher</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/oliz\